  {"category":"aptitude","topic":"ratio_proportion","question":"In a mixture of 60L, ratio of milk to water is 2:1. How much water to add to make ratio 1:2?","options":[{"text":"60L","isCorrect":true},{"text":"40L","isCorrect":false},{"text":"30L","isCorrect":false},{"text":"50L","isCorrect":false}],"correctAnswer":0,"explanation":"Milk=40L, Water=20L. Need 40/(20+x)=1/2. 80=20+x. x=60L","difficulty":"medium","marks":1},
